-- title:
--   Gauss integrality forces 𝔭-integrality at height-one primes above q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$ with $q \nmid N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, and a number field $K$, realised as a finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Let $C_K$ denote the ring `jIntegralClosure (N * q) A K`, that is, the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those series that lie in `fieldOver (N * q) K` — the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $N q$, i.e. the expansions of $j$ and $j_{Nq}$ — and are integral over `jRing A K`. Let $\mathfrak p \subset C_K$ be a prime ideal of height $1$ whose image contains the natural number $q$. Let $g$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$Nq$ modular function field inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume: the series $g$ lies in `fieldOver (N * q) K`; $g$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (N * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation away from the kernel of the reduction induced by $red$ of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ and by `jqModC`, `jqNModC` at level $Nq$ (that is, $g \cdot s = r$ for some $r, s$ in that subring with $s$ not in that kernel); and the image of $g$ under `atkinLehnerBar N q`, the automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` induced by the partial Atkin–Lehner involution `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N q`, lies in the same localisation. The conclusion is that there exist $r, s \in C_K$ with $s \notin \mathfrak p$ and $g \cdot s = r$ as Laurent series, i.e. $g$ lies in the localisation of $C_K$ at $\mathfrak p$.
--
--   In valuation-theoretic form this says that a height-one prime of the level-$Nq$ normalisation $C_K$ lying over $q$ sees only the two Gauss prolongations attached to $A$ and to its partial Atkin–Lehner twist: integrality with respect to both of them already forces integrality at $\mathfrak p$. It is used in the analysis of the rings of integers at the nodes of the special fibre at $q$, in particular by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_mul_eq_mem_jIntegralClosure_of_mem_nodeIntegersOver_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_mul_eq_mem_jIntegralClosure_of_mem_nodeIntegersOver_of_sp_eq_spPlace) and by the two results on local and Noetherian properties of `nodeIntegersOver`.
